<title>HONG KONG: First SIA B777 rolled out in U.S.</title>
<headline>First SIA B777 rolled out in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The first of up to 61 Boeing 777 twin-jets for Singapore Airlines (SIA), powered by Rolls-Royce (R-R) Trent 800 engines, has been rolled out from its U.S. factory, said an R-R statement.</p>
<p>SIA's has ordered 30 777s with another 31 on option, together with US$1.8 billion worth of Rolls-Royce Trent engines.</p>
<p>R-R said the Trent 800 has won more than 30 percent of the world market for 777 engines. The Trent 700, which powers the Airbus A330 twin-jet, has secured 45 percent of engine orders in the Asia-Pacific region, R-R added.</p>
<p>SIA's first 777 is expected to enter service next month, R-R said.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706; fax +5017</p>
